name":"No demand","d":"2026-09-28","pol":-1,"sig":0.72,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"No supply","d":"2026-10-07","pol":1,"sig":0.44,"tier":"low"}],"asof":null},"scores":{"overall":46,"group":"SIC 283x (Chemicals & Pharma)","group_rank":75,"group_n":239,"sector_rank":109,"sector_n":374,"earn":19}},"biz":{"name":"Surrozen, Inc./DE","desc":"Surrozen, Inc., a biotechnology company, discovers and develops product candidates to selectively modulate the Wnt pathway for tissue repair. Its lead product candidates are antibody-based therapeutics that target various disease areas, including diseases of the eye, intestine, liver, lung, retina, kidney, cochlea, cornea, skin, pancreas, and central nervous system. The company develops SZN-814, which combines Frizzled 4 (Fzd4 agonism) and vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF antagonism) to treat diabetic macular edema (DME), neovascular age-related macular degeneration (wet AMD), and retinopathy indications; SZN-8143, which combines Fzd4 agonism, VEGF antagonism, and interleukin-6, or IL-6 for the treatment of DME/wet AMD/uveitic macular edema; and SZN-413, a Fzd4 targeted bi-specific antibody for the treatment of retinal vascular associated diseases. Surrozen, Inc. has a collaboration and license agreement with Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH to research, develop, and commercialize Fzd4 bi-specific antibodies; and a research collaboration agreement with TCGFB, Inc. to discover antibody therapeutics targeting transforming growth factor beta, or TGF-ß, for the treatment of patients with idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis. Surrozen, Inc. was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in South San Francisco, California.","desc_src":"Yahoo Finance profile via yfinance (third-party)","sic":"2836","sic_desc":"Biological Products, (No Diagnostic Substances)","sector":"Healthcare","industry":"Biotechnology","mcap":344614304,"mcap_src":"Yahoo Finance profile (third-party, cached)","hq":"SOUTH SAN FRANCISCO, CA","exchange":"XNAS","fy_end":"12